  "id": "COMPOUND:223 - PROTEIN:1380",
  "verbalization": "Aminosalicylic acid appears to have a shared target with ATP synthase subunit a through a series of intermediate targets, including Diacylglycerol kinase gamma and Fibrauretinoside A. These intermediates are each identified as targets of different compounds, with Aminosalicylic acid linking to Diacylglycerol kinase gamma, which in turn links to ATP synthase subunit a. The evidence suggests a potential pathway where Aminosalicylic acid may modulate the activity of Diacylglycerol kinase gamma, which then influences ATP synthase subunit a. This mechanism is supported by the consistent presence of ATP synthase subunit a as a target across multiple pathways, indicating a possible functional relationship. The integration of these findings highlights a possible role for Aminosalicylic acid in regulating ATP synthase activity through a series of intermediate targets, potentially involving lipid metabolism and enzyme regulation.",
